 ALTERNATIVES: running `run_pending` inside the door's request, rejected because a serve may take ninety seconds and the door's import guard forbids the process launcher it would reach; a separate process started by `remedy ui`, rejected because nothing would then stop its previews when the server closes and it would need its own lifecycle; a new event on the job's stream for each preview state, rejected for now because the card reads one small view and every new event name needs its humanize entry and its readers named, which T003 can add if the card needs them; revalidating by reading `runtime.json` rather than probing, rejected because a running record says nothing about whether the app still answers.
 
 HOW TO REVERSE: delete `packages/orchestration/preview_worker.py` and its test, the door clause, `_dispatch_job_preview`, the `preview` endpoint, the worker in `start_ui_server`, the two ids in `UI_EXPOSED_COMMANDS`, the config key and its guide line, the additions to `preview_control.py` and their tests, the guard edits in `tests/ui_server/test_command_channel.py` and `tests/ui_server/test_preview_commands.py`, and this paragraph.
+
+## DECISION F041 D5 — the cockpit shows a job's results in a Results panel opened from the right panel: the README fragment through one inserting site whose images are rewritten to the file route or dropped to their text, a screenshot grid that opens a lightbox, and an app card that polls the preview view while it is on screen and sends the preview pair through the write door (2026-09-29)
+
+CONTEXT: T003 asks for the part of F041 a person sees. Measured by the reviewer at `d735c058`: `apps/ui/src` holds no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, and only a comment in `ForceBrainGraph.tsx` names `innerHTML`; the vitest configuration collects `src/**/*.test.ts` in a node environment with no DOM, so a rule inside a component ships untested and components are pinned as source by `tests/ui_contracts/`; the story, the tour and the lessons open from quiet buttons in `RightLivePanel.tsx`, and `RemedyShell.tsx` mounts each as a sibling after `</main>`, portaled to `document.body`; every read door in `apps/ui/src/api/remedyApi.ts` takes one injected fetcher and one decoder and never throws, and every write goes through a `*Send.ts` module whose request carries the bearer token, the CSRF header and a minted nonce; every API route of the UI server reads its token from the query string, so an image the cockpit shows from the file route carries the token in its own URL; the sanitizer keeps a README image only as `<img src="<path>" alt="<text>">` with a path and no scheme, while the file route serves `README.md` and `captures/<name>` alone; the component specification puts an "Open app" button in the task detail, while a preview belongs to the whole job; and the reference describes no lightbox.
+
+CHOSEN: (1) THE ENTRY is a `Results` button in `RightLivePanel.tsx` directly after `Story`, and `RemedyShell.tsx` mounts `ArtifactsPanel` after the story, outside `<main>`. (2) THE PURE RULES live in `apps/ui/src/api/artifactPreview.ts`: the decoders of the artifacts view and the preview view, which answer null for any payload out of shape; the three paths; `readmeCockpitHtml`, which points a README image at the file route when its path names a listed capture and writes its alt text in its place otherwise; the caption a capture's file name gives; the lightbox's next index, which stops at both ends; the app card's words, action and link for each state, where a link is offered only while live and only to an http or https address; and the poll delay, two seconds while starting or probing and fifteen otherwise. (3) THE SEND is `apps/ui/src/api/previewSend.ts`, built as `pauseSend.ts` is and composing its submit, with sentences of its own. (4) THE READS are `loadArtifactsView` and `loadPreviewView` in `remedyApi.ts`, shaped as the tour door. (5) THE PANEL is `components/artifacts/ArtifactsPanel.tsx`, a region portaled to the document body, holding the app card, the README through the one `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` of `apps/ui/src` with an "Open the full README" link when it was cut, and the screenshot grid; `ArtifactLightbox.tsx` is a separate portaled dialog that the arrow keys step and Escape closes; `AppPreviewCard.tsx` reads the preview view while the page is visible, with one timer whose effect is keyed on plain values only, so every read while the card is on screen counts as a viewer and a closed panel or a hidden page lets the idle stop run. (6) THE ORDER: this round lands (1) to (5) with a headless render; the next lands the result tour's preview anchor and the end-to-end run on a fixture app, and the closure follows.
+
+ALTERNATIVES: an "Open app" button in the task detail as the component specification draws it, rejected because a preview runs the whole job's project and the detail belongs to one task, which the assumption log records; a new tab of the evidence panel, rejected for the same reason, because that panel shows one task run; rewriting README images on the server, rejected because the server would have to write the caller's token into the fragment; parsing the fragment in the browser, rejected because the cockpit's tests have no DOM and the server's output has one fixed image shape; polling while the panel is closed, rejected because the idle stop exists for a preview nobody is looking at.
+
+HOW TO REVERSE: delete `apps/ui/src/api/artifactPreview.ts`, `apps/ui/src/api/previewSend.ts`, the directory `apps/ui/src/components/artifacts/`, their tests, `tests/ui_contracts/test_artifact_preview.py`, the two doors in `remedyApi.ts`, the button in `RightLivePanel.tsx`, the state and the mount in `RemedyShell.tsx`, the assumption log's F041 line and this paragraph.
